From 52db7e59e3d2d94079d4d67a292f769b65abd014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 07:57:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Implement zwp_idle_inhibit_manager_v1

Owl doesn't track per-surface visibility/occlusion, so this counts
every live inhibitor object as active (the spec explicitly allows
"counting mapped inhibitors" as a v1-adequate approximation) and
holds a single system power assertion for as long as that count is
above zero, mirroring OwlWpContentType's per-surface destroy-listener
bookkeeping for lifetime tracking.

Three build configurations: IOPMAssertionCreateWithName with
kIOPMAssertionTypeNoDisplaySleep on 10.6+ (the new OWL_HAS_IOPM
feature flag; deliberately not the newer
kIOPMAssertionTypePreventUserIdleDisplaySleep alias, which only
exists since 10.7 and fails to build against the 10.6 SDK), a
periodic UpdateSystemActivity() timer as the pre-IOPM Apple fallback,
and a tracked-but-inert no-op on GNUstep, which has neither API.
Links IOKit and CoreServices normally (unlike IOSurface, both exist
on every supported OS version, so no need to weak_framework them).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X4132h4W4m6yZEz9BE7yN4
